          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "দায়ী (dāyī) is Sanskrit dāyin, which Monier-Williams gives as giving and also as owing or having to pay. Bengali uses it for the one who owes an answer, the one to blame; that narrower sense is not one the dictionary gives. দায়িত্ব, a responsibility, is its abstract."
            }
          ]
        },
